{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"carveNavigationMesh","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It will still be affected by further postprocessing of the baking process, like edge and polygon simplification.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Requires ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/NavigationObstacle2D\/affectNavigationMesh","type":"reference"},{"text":" to be enabled.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If enabled the obstacle vertices will carve into the baked navigation mesh with the shape unaffected by additional offsets (e.g. agent radius)."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/NavigationObstacle2D"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/navigationobstacle2d\/carvenavigationmesh"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"carveNavigationMesh"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"symbolKind":"property","title":"carveNavigationMesh","externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot20NavigationObstacle2DC05carveC4MeshSbvp","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/NavigationObstacle2D\/carveNavigationMesh","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/NavigationObstacle2D/carveNavigationMesh":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/navigationobstacle2d\/carvenavigationmesh","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"carveNavigationMesh","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"carveNavigationMesh","abstract":[{"text":"If enabled the obstacle vertices will carve into the baked navigation mesh with the shape unaffected by additional offsets (e.g. agent radius).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/NavigationObstacle2D\/carveNavigationMesh"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/NavigationObstacle2D/affectNavigationMesh":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/navigationobstacle2d\/affectnavigationmesh","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"affectNavigationMesh","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"affectNavigationMesh","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If enabled and parsed in a navigation mesh baking process the obstacle will discard source geometry inside its "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/NavigationObstacle2D\/vertices","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" defined shape."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/NavigationObstacle2D\/affectNavigationMesh"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/NavigationObstacle2D":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/NavigationObstacle2D","role":"symbol","title":"NavigationObstacle2D","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"2D obstacle used to affect navigation mesh baking or constrain velocities of avoidance controlled agents."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/navigationobstacle2d","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NavigationObstacle2D"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NavigationObstacle2D"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/NavigationObstacle2D/vertices":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/NavigationObstacle2D\/vertices","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"vertices","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"vertices","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot18PackedVector2ArrayC","text":"PackedVector2Array"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The outline vertices of the obstacle. If the vertices are winded in clockwise order agents will be pushed in by the obstacle, else they will be pushed out. Outlines can not be crossed or overlap. Should the vertices using obstacle be warped to a new position agent’s can not predict this movement and may get trapped inside the obstacle."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/navigationobstacle2d\/vertices"}}}